# Commit-message validation is opt-in (disabled by default, like pre-commit).
# Uncomment the line below to enforce the team commit convention: Conventional
# Commits shape, the 72-char ceiling, no vague subjects, and a mandatory Jira
# reference (ABC-<number>) in the subject. The validator ships with the coredoc
# plugin; it only inspects the message — never your tree — and prints the exact
# reason on failure.
# node plugins/coredoc/scripts/validate-commit-message.mjs --file "$1" || exit 1
